      "updated": 1785771804049,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Public IPv4 address\nattached.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Public IPv4 address\nattached.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4BWipn1F9Wy6h9PEufGu7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2088.7553483576967,
      "y": 13823.49606034308,
      "width": 1045,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIx",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1453771504,
      "version": 662,
      "versionNonce": 1281405456,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785772182142,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every EC2 instance get a new public IPv4 , every time we stop and start it.\nApart from the public IPv4 there is something like a private IPv4 that can be attached by\nAWS. Private IPv4 can be used on private networks such as AWS internal working. This is not\ngoing to accessible across the internet. this can be used for some internal working or internal\ncommunication on the services or instances. Private IPv4 stays attached to our EC2 instance\neven if we start and stop them again. But public IP address can totally change.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Every EC2 instance get a new public IPv4 , every time we stop and start it.\nApart from the public IPv4 there is something like a private IPv4 that can be attached by\nAWS. Private IPv4 can be used on private networks such as AWS internal working. This is not\ngoing to accessible across the internet. this can be used for some internal working or internal\ncommunication on the services or instances. Private IPv4 stays attached to our EC2 instance\neven if we start and stop them again. But public IP address can totally change.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pI0Jpy_dXniO8PQ5vvusU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2049.8842546076967,
      "y": 14052.86324784308,
      "width": 110,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIy",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 860826640,
      "version": 17,
      "versionNonce": 12942576,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785772202869,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2 IPv6 -> ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2 IPv6 -> ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "myKrKhAnJMMU__4-BJdSw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2105.3295671076967,
      "y": 14082.72262284308,
      "width": 1023,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 710869232,
      "version": 398,
      "versionNonce": 1345702928,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785772403729,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "there is a support of IPv6 address as well -> newer version of IP that help us to get \nallocated with a couple of IP address, this is the free allocation all together. LIke\nwe can get IPv6 address alltogether free in AWS without paying any charge. These IPv6 address\nare public in AWS so most of the IPv6 address that we are going to find those will be \npublic.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "there is a support of IPv6 address as well -> newer version of IP that help us to get \nallocated with a couple of IP address, this is the free allocation all together. LIke\nwe can get IPv6 address alltogether free in AWS without paying any charge. These IPv6 address\nare public in AWS so most of the IPv6 address that we are going to find those will be \npublic.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Ztho0l5ZGrofw__8hT19W",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2044.2006608576967,
      "y": 14289.47262284308,
      "width": 176,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJ0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1964902416,
      "version": 21,
      "versionNonce": 1395511024,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785772506534,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3 Elastic IP -> ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3 Elastic IP -> ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Duu5vQEd5c3XZudSbu_ny",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2100.1459733576967,
      "y": 14326.95309159308,
      "width": 1012,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJ1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1092179472,
      "version": 397,
      "versionNonce": 992873299,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785856523763,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "using elastic IP we can attach a fix IPv4 address to our EC2 instance. we can create elastic\nIP using elastic IP service and attach to our EC2. This is going to our fix IP address it is\nnot going to change. IF we will terminate and again start new EC2 then our Elastic IP and\npublic IP would be same.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "using elastic IP we can attach a fix IPv4 address to our EC2 instance. we can create elastic\nIP using elastic IP service and attach to our EC2. This is going to our fix IP address it is\nnot going to change. IF we will terminate and again start new EC2 then our Elastic IP and\npublic IP would be same.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "X3nocfJ80NP8c0voCaRRp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2376.0287858576967,
      "y": 14442.40621659308,
      "width": 11,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
