      "seed": 2057325011,
      "version": 73,
      "versionNonce": 1377753149,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785856714165,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "VPC(Virtual Private Cloud) -> ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "VPC(Virtual Private Cloud) -> ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hc6iTCN2zv19RRcnB7gbD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2095.9623796076967,
      "y": 14576.90231034308,
      "width": 1078,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJ4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 382823763,
      "version": 612,
      "versionNonce": 613795859,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785857198148,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Using VPC we can prepare a private network to deploy our resources. Private network is logically\nisolated virtual network in AWS cloud. and within this VPC we can launch our resources like EC2,\nS3, databases etc, they will be available only inside our VPC. On top of it we can launch actually\nmultiple layer of security including there is something called as Security Group, network which\ncan help us to control our EC2 within our VPC.\n\nWithin a VPC there is concept called as Subnet.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Using VPC we can prepare a private network to deploy our resources. Private network is logically\nisolated virtual network in AWS cloud. and within this VPC we can launch our resources like EC2,\nS3, databases etc, they will be available only inside our VPC. On top of it we can launch actually\nmultiple layer of security including there is something called as Security Group, network which\ncan help us to control our EC2 within our VPC.\n\nWithin a VPC there is concept called as Subnet.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "1_jlvqF44b2R9NY7PHoCC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2092.8295671076967,
      "y": 14791.72262284308,
      "width": 110,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJ5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 508857245,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 1725605917,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785856956115,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Subnet -> ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Subnet -> ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TUo_SBJYPRcqyoXAtOiCr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2139.0053483576967,
      "y": 14821.37496659308,
      "width": 1067,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJ6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1967153469,
      "version": 379,
      "versionNonce": 1874589533,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785857125547,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A Subnet helps us to create partition in our VPC, Inside a subnet there will be a range of IP\naddresses available. we can say our VPC will be having bunch of IPs and then we can create subnet\nout of it so that we can partition our VPC and we can do this partition across regions.\nWe can create public and private subnets.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A Subnet helps us to create partition in our VPC, Inside a subnet there will be a range of IP\naddresses available. we can say our VPC will be having bunch of IPs and then we can create subnet\nout of it so that we can partition our VPC and we can do this partition across regions.\nWe can create public and private subnets.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
