      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785857929732,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why we want to partition our VPC into subnet/s? Why we even want to create subnet?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why we want to partition our VPC into subnet/s? Why we even want to create subnet?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "0MhksMmpfpi-Nz2NrJ-1A",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2478.8295671076967,
      "y": 16500.72262284308,
      "width": 11,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJc",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1316110813,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 941512115,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785857887284,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ijLt3f8xXCUerqAB5NqF8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2006.2240983576967,
      "y": 16534.95699784308,
      "width": 1122,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 555566813,
      "version": 974,
      "versionNonce": 712157373,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785858347376,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "there are some resources that we want to accessible through internet ex -> EC2, lets say we have \ndeployed some server on it and server depends on some kind of a database. If it is depending on some\nkind of database, this database doesn't need to be explicitly exposed to the internet. Server can only\ninteract with Database noone else. these resources that we don't want to expose in internet, we can \nhost in private subnets then these resources will be only available inside our private subnet.\nFrom the public subnet we can still communicate with the private subnet but nobody on the internet \nwill be able to directly communicate to the private subnet.\n\nThis public subnet if it has to get access to internet, it uses something called as internet gateway",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "there are some resources that we want to accessible through internet ex -> EC2, lets say we have \ndeployed some server on it and server depends on some kind of a database. If it is depending on some\nkind of database, this database doesn't need to be explicitly exposed to the internet. Server can only\ninteract with Database noone else. these resources that we don't want to expose in internet, we can \nhost in private subnets then these resources will be only available inside our private subnet.\nFrom the public subnet we can still communicate with the private subnet but nobody on the internet \nwill be able to directly communicate to the private subnet.\n\nThis public subnet if it has to get access to internet, it uses something called as internet gateway",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "b9a5QIiMGFHc-8UvvfwG4",
